        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "73428fb2-4e46-3e1d-9b5b-918e41e4e15e",
                "word": "vélocipède",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3889f4c0-185e-47c2-9d85-2f52e228c52f",
                        "entry_id": "73428fb2-4e46-3e1d-9b5b-918e41e4e15e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "vélocipèdes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b14bf54f-21f9-336d-9ec6-87c468e2d252",
                        "entry_id": "73428fb2-4e46-3e1d-9b5b-918e41e4e15e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Appareil de locomotion dont on met les roues en mouvement avec les pieds."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "86bda845-adb3-43ed-9708-43a82aaae264",
                                "sense_id": "b14bf54f-21f9-336d-9ec6-87c468e2d252",
                                "text": "[…] : j’ai photographié des chevaux, des ânes, des chiens, des hommes à pied ou des vélocipèdes ; […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbf6a572-9bd2-4462-bafe-0c4a48ec844d",
                                "sense_id": "b14bf54f-21f9-336d-9ec6-87c468e2d252",
                                "text": "Dans le parc de Saint-Cloud, le 31 mai 1868, se déroulent les premières courses officielles de vélocipèdes."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c590d2fc-427b-410b-9727-63ed3996f36d",
                                "sense_id": "b14bf54f-21f9-336d-9ec6-87c468e2d252",
                                "text": "En fait, comme le montre Philippe Gaboriau, le vélocipède a connu trois moments de mode au XIXᵉ siècle. Dès 1818, le vélocipède du baron Karl Drais von Sauerbroom ^([sic]) avait été le support d'une mode éphémère et extravagante parmi les dandys et les aristocrates de Paris et de Londres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "74359423-7728-4381-97d0-5b4acff3bcc8",
                                "sense_id": "b14bf54f-21f9-336d-9ec6-87c468e2d252",
                                "text": "Mélie pareil : quatre ou cinq ans pour offrir à son Alphonse, qui est mécanicien de son métier et maquereautin d'occasion, les moyens d'ouvrir un atelier de vélocipèdes ou de bicyclettes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eb254cc1-c548-370e-b519-6b7c8c113c72",
                        "entry_id": "73428fb2-4e46-3e1d-9b5b-918e41e4e15e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Bicyclette ; vélo."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1ef9f3d-7b0d-4a32-93b3-0b50a1537763",
                                "sense_id": "eb254cc1-c548-370e-b519-6b7c8c113c72",
                                "text": "Il y avait un manège de vélocipèdes. Blanche, avec ses manies de faire toujours à sa tête, chahutait là-dessus en montrant ses mollets et tout. On lui avait dit : Ne fais donc pas ça, tu verras qu’un jour ou l’autre tu te feras ramasser. Ça y était : qu’est-ce que j’avais dit ! Au Dépôt, il y a la visite, elle n’avait pas passé saine et on l’avait envoyée se soigner à Saint-Lazare."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce623f2f-7ea7-4716-8471-2336c31547ef",
                                "sense_id": "eb254cc1-c548-370e-b519-6b7c8c113c72",
                                "text": "[…] ; ces appareils ont une très grande roue devant et une toute petite derrière ; on les appelle des araignées ou des “grands bis” j'en vois sur la route de Villecresnes quand il y a des courses de vélocipèdes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7a77a66b-d441-478d-86dd-5159e7223c3b",
                        "source_entry_id": "73428fb2-4e46-3e1d-9b5b-918e41e4e15e",
                        "target_lang_word": "bicycle",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bicycle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "129f68f4-1c0d-3312-bb13-e5d5507f00b3",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A vehicle that has two primary wheels, one behind the other, a steering handle, and a saddle seat or seats and is usually propelled by the action of a rider’s feet upon pedals."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e030eaf6-03f7-4415-89b9-f5ff4a86399b",
                                                "sense_id": "129f68f4-1c0d-3312-bb13-e5d5507f00b3",
                                                "text": "In most English villages, as we are informed, bicycles are not allowed on the sidewalks; and the hand-books issued by English manufacturers of bicycles caution their customers that it is a forbidden practice, while in many places bells have to be attached to the bicycles even when ridden in the streets."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c12ac9cc-514c-3293-8ce0-d0eccf1766ec",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any similar vehicle powered by human pedaling or steered with a handlebar, regardless of the number of wheels."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "058b5002-078f-4a6c-bdb5-9b2f6b7d69b0",
                                                "sense_id": "c12ac9cc-514c-3293-8ce0-d0eccf1766ec",
                                                "text": "The small, three-wheeled bicycle-type vehicle is probably the lowest-cost set of wheels for routine, in-park patrol use."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a9587301-50e3-3711-a27b-fb39d3a7a29e",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A traveling block used on a cable in skidding logs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fd2c2268-ceaa-3151-ab87-2392327af995",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The best possible hand in lowball."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7bab9923-6a12-317f-8788-79146f9c0c58",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A motorbike."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Australia",
                                            "British",
                                            "New-Zealand"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ff48e9a-a707-308f-9091-4a75b8734e07",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A slut; a promiscuous woman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "vulgar"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4edc036e-256b-40f1-b681-d5d69e99d3eb",
                                                "sense_id": "4ff48e9a-a707-308f-9091-4a75b8734e07",
                                                "text": "‘What sort of bullying does this sergeant go in for?’ ‘Character assassination,’ she said in a matter-of-fact tone that belied the very real difficulties it was causing her. ‘There’s a lot of whispering about slags and tarts behind my back and sniggers whenever I appear. Half of the men seem to think I’m a dyke who needs curing, the other half think I’m the platoon bicycle. [...]’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ea159fa0-af88-39e6-9081-0249c6354a73",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A stabilizing technique in which one foot is pushed down while the other is pulled up."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7029078e-e611-3c4a-8319-8f8a526b06a5",
                                        "entry_id": "7aeca5e9-788b-3db1-80fe-341beee50014",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The wheel: either the lowest straight (A-2-3-4-5) or the best low hand in Lowball or High-low poker."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bicycle",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "98bed318-f0ca-3412-a9f0-e5359bfe5204",
                                        "entry_id": "73995974-26e8-36fa-aa32-f70614cb518c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To travel or exercise using a bicycle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "efc1d251-31f4-4196-aeea-c24af5e7cbc4",
                                                "sense_id": "98bed318-f0ca-3412-a9f0-e5359bfe5204",
                                                "text": "“At least it cannot be your health,\" said he, as his keen eyes darted over her; \"so ardent a bicyclist must be full of energy.” […] “Yes, I bicycle a good deal, Mr. Holmes, and that has something to do with my visit to you to-day.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1aa24553-feac-33d7-bca7-ee5307ca0669",
                                        "entry_id": "73995974-26e8-36fa-aa32-f70614cb518c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To physically ship (a recorded programme) to another broadcasting entity."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a7974531-40b2-452a-9456-a788de2eabf5",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa24553-feac-33d7-bca7-ee5307ca0669",
                                                "text": "“Bicycling” defeated the possibility of topicality, a prime production habit of the network-trained production executives staffing the new entity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64656158-6432-4c7b-b068-ac16744ef3c5",
                                                "sense_id": "1aa24553-feac-33d7-bca7-ee5307ca0669",
                                                "text": "In turn, two-inch tapes of these could be “bicycled” from one place to another across the country, thereby altering and improving production economies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
